1. DEFINITIONS
==============================================

"Software" means the Fragmented Encrypted Container System (FECS), including 
all source code, object code, documentation, specifications, and associated 
materials, whether in source or object form.

"Licensor" means Purn Vadodariya.

"Licensee" means any individual, entity, organization, or legal person that 
obtains, accesses, downloads, installs, or uses the Software in any manner.

"Commercial Use" means any use of the Software that is primarily intended 
for or directed toward commercial advantage, monetary compensation, or 
business operations, including but not limited to:
  (a) Use in a commercial product or service
  (b) Use in a for-profit organization
  (c) Use to generate revenue or profit
  (d) Use to support commercial activities
  (e) Use in a business or enterprise environment

"Derivative Work" means any work based upon or incorporating the Software, 
including modifications, enhancements, adaptations, translations, or any 
other changes to the Software.

"Distribution" means any act of making the Software available to third 
parties, including but not limited to:
  (a) Copying, transferring, or sharing
  (b) Uploading or downloading
  (c) Selling, renting, or leasing
  (d) Providing access through networks
  (e) Embedding in other software

"Confidential Information" means all information disclosed or made available 
by the Licensor to the Licensee, including but not limited to:
  (a) Software code and algorithms
  (b) Technical specifications and documentation
  (c) Business strategies and plans
  (d) Security protocols and mechanisms
  (e) Trade secrets and proprietary methods

"Main Header" means the primary header structure containing critical 
metadata for file reconstruction.

"Recovery Header" means the secondary header structure enabling file 
recovery in case of corruption.

"Authenticated Encryption" means encryption that simultaneously provides 
confidentiality, integrity, and authenticity.

